meta {
  name: Subscription - Accept Cancellation Offer
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/billing/subscription/cancellation/accept-offer
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "offer": "discount",
    "reason": "too_expensive",
    "comment": "Optional free text."
  }
}

docs {
  The customer stays and takes the offer shown for their reason. Requires
  the `billing.manage` permission.

  `offer` is `discount` (applies the discount to the Stripe subscription,
  alongside any discount it already holds) or `help` (alerts the team with
  the comment). The offer is worked out again on the server: `422` when it
  is not the one currently available for `reason`, including a second
  discount inside the cooldown. `downgrade` is always `422` here, because it
  is taken on the plans screen.

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { outcome, percent_off, months, subscription } }`.
}
